WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.862
Olopa plot. A computer voice is reading this.

2
00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:12.305
In March and April, your land usually has little plant cover. The satellite saw it from 2021 to 2025.

3
00:00:12.555 --> 00:00:17.955
In 1 of the last 15 years there were fires within half a kilometer of your plot, in April.

4
00:00:18.205 --> 00:00:24.617
In the last 25 years, the midsummer drought never brought more than 15 days in a row with almost no rain.

5
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:38.326
This year, July and August got only a fifth of the normal rain (22 %). That is less than in 1997, the driest year since 1991. It is a preliminary figure.

6
00:00:38.576 --> 00:00:44.731
Today, all three options come out even: what you plant today, maize with jack bean and short-cycle maize.

7
00:00:44.981 --> 00:01:01.324
NASA computes 33 possible climates for 2041 to 2060. Planting as today, maize with beans has enough water in 9 of 33. Maize with jack bean: in 9. Short-cycle maize: in all 33.

8
00:01:01.574 --> 00:01:05.447
This is not an official notice: talk it over with your extension worker.
